From: krun-gaming
Subject: [PATCH] drm/virtio: dumb buffers as guest blobs also with 3D

A Venus-only host (no GL renderer, e.g. virglrenderer on macOS) cannot create
classic 2D resources, so dumb buffers (Xorg modesetting, fbcon) failed with
ERR_UNSPEC. Guest blobs need nothing from the host renderer.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_gem.c	2026-11-08 03:55:48
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_gem.c	2026-11-08 03:55:48
@@ -81,7 +81,12 @@
 	params.size = args->size;
 	params.dumb = true;
 
-	if (vgdev->has_resource_blob && !vgdev->has_virgl_3d) {
+	/*
+	 * Guest blobs need nothing from the host renderer. With 3D (e.g. a
+	 * Venus-only host without a GL renderer) classic 2D resources may not
+	 * be creatable at all, so use guest blobs whenever blobs are supported.
+	 */
+	if (vgdev->has_resource_blob) {
 		params.blob_mem = VIRTGPU_BLOB_MEM_GUEST;
 		params.blob_flags = VIRTGPU_BLOB_FLAG_USE_SHAREABLE;
 		params.blob = true;
